## GOAL
  To learn the fundamental networking framework that determines the various stages in which data is handled across a network

## SUMMARY
  OSI (= Open Systems Interconnection model)
    Model used in networking to provide a framework for any kind of device (different functions and design) as long as the informations follow the uniformity of the model.
    It has 7 layers, each of them having a different set of responsabilities :
      7. Application
      6. Presentation
      5. Session
      4. Transport
      3. Network
      2. Data link
      1. Physical
    The event of every individual data going through each layers, pieces of information added to the data, is called ENCAPSULATION.

  1. PHYSICAL Layer
    Physical components of the hardware : Cables (Ethernet...), connectors...
    Devices use binary to transfer data between them.

  2. DATA LINK Layer
    In each network-enable device, there's a NIC (= Network Interface Card) holding the MAC address. 
    The MAC address is "Burned" into the NIC, meaning it can't be changed, if we move the NIC on another device, the MAC address moves with it.
    The goal to the Data Link layer is to classify those informations to present the datas in a format suitable for transmission.

